-- Social Security (Personal Independence Payment) Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/377)
-- NOUNS: the enumerations and records that more than one module needs.
-- Declarations only: no rule and no #EVAL here.
--
-- Source: uksi-2013-377.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script
-- from legislation.gov.uk (version 2026-04-30). It is not the official text.
--
-- Every top-level name in this encoding is specific to what it decides, because
-- two modules that define one name cannot be imported together; pip-seat.l4
-- imports every module.

§ `Nouns of the Regulations`

-- reg 2 "component": the daily living component or, as the case may be, the
-- mobility component of personal independence payment.
DECLARE `a component of personal independence payment` IS ONE OF
    `the daily living component`
    `the mobility component`

-- regs 4(3), 5(3), 6(3): the two levels of ability the assessment can find.
-- A person who has neither is the third constructor.
DECLARE `a level of ability to carry out activities` IS ONE OF
    `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`
    `limited ability`
    `severely limited ability`

-- reg 24 and regs 12(1), 12(2), 13(1), 13(2): the two rates of a component, and
-- the case in which no rate of it is awarded.
DECLARE `a rate of a component` IS ONE OF
    `no rate of the component`
    `the standard rate of the component`
    `the enhanced rate of the component`

-- reg 2 "adult disability payment", "child disability payment", "Scottish adult
-- disability living allowance", "disability living allowance"; regs 15, 15A, 15B,
-- 26 and 26A speak of a previous award of one of them. No rule of the text reads
-- the disability living allowance constructor; it is named because reg 2 defines it.
-- out of text: the Scottish regulations and the Social Security Contributions and
-- Benefits Act 1992 s 71 say what each benefit is.
DECLARE `the benefit paid under an earlier award` IS ONE OF
    `personal independence payment`
    `adult disability payment`
    `child disability payment`
    `Scottish adult disability living allowance`
    `disability living allowance`
    `some other benefit`

-- Schedule 1: the activities, the letters of the descriptors, the descriptors of
-- each activity and one row for each descriptor. Generated from the table lines of
-- the text by a script that is not kept in this folder; the figures are copied, not typed.
DECLARE `an activity of Schedule 1` IS ONE OF
    `daily living activity 1, preparing food`
    `daily living activity 2, taking nutrition`
    `daily living activity 3, managing therapy or monitoring a health condition`
    `daily living activity 4, washing and bathing`
    `daily living activity 5, managing toilet needs or incontinence`
    `daily living activity 6, dressing and undressing`
    `daily living activity 7, communicating verbally`
    `daily living activity 8, reading and understanding signs, symbols and words`
    `daily living activity 9, engaging with other people face to face`
    `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions`
    `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`
    `mobility activity 2, moving around`

DECLARE `a letter of a descriptor` IS ONE OF
    `letter a`
    `letter b`
    `letter c`
    `letter d`
    `letter e`
    `letter f`
    `letter g`

DECLARE `a descriptor of daily living activity 1` IS ONE OF
